SET MATRIX ZEROS

BRUTE 
TRANSVERSE MATRIX
WHENEVER YOU FIND A 0 MARK ALL ELEMS IN ITS ROWS AND COLUMN AS -1
AFTER TRAVERSAL CONVERT ALL -1 TO 0



OPTIMAL 
USE FIRST ROW AND FIRST COLUMN AS MARKERS
IF MATRIX[I][J]==0, MARK MAT[I][0]=0 
MAT[0][J]=0

USE COL0 TO SEPERATLY TRACK WHETHER THE FIRST COLUMN SHOULD BECOME ZERO
TRAVERSE FROM BOTTOM RIGHT TO TOP LEFT AND SET ZEROS USING MARKERS


def setmat(self, mat):
    rows = len(mat)
    cols = len(mat[0])
    col0 = 1

    # Step 1: Mark zeros
    for i in range(rows):
        if mat[i][0] == 0:
            col0 = 0
        for j in range(1, cols):
            if mat[i][j] == 0:
                mat[i][0] = 0
                mat[0][j] = 0

    # Step 2: Traverse backwards and set zeros
    for i in range(rows - 1, -1, -1):
        for j in range(cols - 1, 0, -1):
            if mat[i][0] == 0 or mat[0][j] == 0:
                mat[i][j] = 0
        if col0 == 0:
            mat[i][0] = 0
